  data: {
    LLM: "Follow the rules: play to foundations when possible, and consider when to play onto the opponent's discard.\n\nTry to place the highest cards possible on your opponent's discard pile; being left with kings in your stock is bad. Remember the order of cards in your face-down stock to decide when to stop laying off onto the opponent and turn a stock card instead.\n\nBalance giving cards to the opponent (to clear your pile) against giving them playable sequences; use knowledge of your stock order to time when to draw.",
